data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"result":{"content":[{"text":"{\"series\":[{\"product_id\":14100287,\"coordinate\":\"1.7.1.1.1.1.0.0.0.0\",\"vector_id\":2062815,\"context\":{\"citation\":\"Statistics Canada. Table 14-10-0287-01, Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle. Vector v2062815. Released 2026-11-06.\",\"table_id\":\"14-10-0287-01\",\"table_url\":\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1410028701\",\"series_title\":\"Canada;Unemployment rate;Total - Gender;15 years and over;Estimate;Seasonally adjusted\",\"unit\":\"Percent\",\"scale\":\"units\",\"frequency\":\"Monthly\",\"geography\":\"Canada\",\"first_period\":\"1976-01-01\",\"last_period\":\"2026-10-01\"},\"observations\":[{\"ref_period\":\"2026-08-01\",\"value\":6.4},{\"ref_period\":\"2026-09-01\",\"value\":6.5},{\"ref_period\":\"2026-10-01\",\"value\":6.7}]}],\"provenance\":{\"source\":\"statcan-wds\",\"url\":\"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorsAndLatestNPeriods\",\"licence\":\"Statistics Canada Open Licence (https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence)\",\"commercial_use\":\"allowed\",\"caveats\":[\"LFS and SEPH employment are different measures: do not compare their levels. The LFS is a household survey that counts employed people (a person with two jobs counts once), including the self-employed and agriculture; SEPH counts payroll jobs, so it leaves out the self-employed and agriculture, fishing and trapping, private household services, religious organisations and military personnel of the defence services. LFS estimates carry sampling error; preliminary SEPH estimates are revised. Compare trends over several months, not one month's change. For earnings in a detailed industry, such as provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912), use SEPH (14-10-0203 monthly, 14-10-0204 annual) and say why: the LFS wage table 14-10-0064 stops at broad sectors ('Public administration' as a whole).\",\"LFS figures are survey estimates. Table 14-10-0287 publishes the standard error of each estimate, of its month-to-month change and of its year-over-year change (the Statistics dimension). A change is significant at the 5% level only when the change plus or minus two standard errors excludes zero, which many small monthly moves do not. Statistics Canada releases estimates with a CV up to 16.5% freely, with a warning up to 33.3%, and not above; estimates under a minimum size (1,500 for Canada) are suppressed. Seasonally adjusted series are revised once a year.\"]},\"detail\":\"brief: pass detail='full' for full provenance and every field; reproduce_code gives scripts that fetch the same data.\"}","type":"text"}],"isError":false,"structuredContent":{"series":[{"product_id":14100287,"coordinate":"1.7.1.1.1.1.0.0.0.0","vector_id":2062815,"context":{"citation":"Statistics Canada. Table 14-10-0287-01, Labour force characteristics, monthly, seasonally adjusted and trend-cycle. Vector v2062815. Released 2026-11-06.","table_id":"14-10-0287-01","table_url":"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1410028701","series_title":"Canada;Unemployment rate;Total - Gender;15 years and over;Estimate;Seasonally adjusted","unit":"Percent","scale":"units","frequency":"Monthly","geography":"Canada","first_period":"1976-01-01","last_period":"2026-10-01"},"observations":[{"ref_period":"2026-08-01","value":6.4},{"ref_period":"2026-09-01","value":6.5},{"ref_period":"2026-10-01","value":6.7}]}],"provenance":{"source":"statcan-wds","url":"https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/wds/rest/getDataFromVectorsAndLatestNPeriods","licence":"Statistics Canada Open Licence (https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence)","commercial_use":"allowed","caveats":["LFS and SEPH employment are different measures: do not compare their levels. The LFS is a household survey that counts employed people (a person with two jobs counts once), including the self-employed and agriculture; SEPH counts payroll jobs, so it leaves out the self-employed and agriculture, fishing and trapping, private household services, religious organisations and military personnel of the defence services. LFS estimates carry sampling error; preliminary SEPH estimates are revised. Compare trends over several months, not one month's change. For earnings in a detailed industry, such as provincial and territorial public administration (NAICS 912), use SEPH (14-10-0203 monthly, 14-10-0204 annual) and say why: the LFS wage table 14-10-0064 stops at broad sectors ('Public administration' as a whole).","LFS figures are survey estimates. Table 14-10-0287 publishes the standard error of each estimate, of its month-to-month change and of its year-over-year change (the Statistics dimension). A change is significant at the 5% level only when the change plus or minus two standard errors excludes zero, which many small monthly moves do not. Statistics Canada releases estimates with a CV up to 16.5% freely, with a warning up to 33.3%, and not above; estimates under a minimum size (1,500 for Canada) are suppressed. Seasonally adjusted series are revised once a year."]},"detail":"brief: pass detail='full' for full provenance and every field; reproduce_code gives scripts that fetch the same data."}}}

